{
  "about": "updateSpec patch rules, shared by the server (crates/boxd-core/src/machine_spec_patch.rs) and both SDKs (sdk/typescript/tests/spec.test.ts, sdk/python/tests/test_spec.py). Each case applies the JSON Merge Patch `patch` to `current` and expects either the checked spec (`result`, stored form) and the changed fields with how each applies (`changes`; `machine` says what the machine is: status, size, its package rows, whether it is a fork; default running 2x8) and, for `packages`, the commands whose rows it skips and un-skips (`skipped`, `unskipped`; none when absent), or the exact error (`error`). With `minimal`, `patch` is also exactly what the SDKs compute from `current` to `result`. Errors with `sdk` are also raised by the SDKs before sending. Change the rules in all three places together.",
